{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779507348,"nonce":"N4YN4KQiMrNHIVw+mwfXsFpzLRY=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ7Jug","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/168","origin":"github"},"title":"Survey efficiency: coverage-area-per-energy from 2026-05-22 mission patterns","message":"## Goal\n\nQuantify BizzyBoat survey efficiency as **coverage-area-per-energy** for the typical mission patterns that students will run during Summer Hydro 2026. End-state: a class-planning rule of thumb (e.g., \"a class cohort can survey N m² per battery at 2 kt with M m line spacing\") backed by 2026-05-22 in-water bag data.\n\n## Method\n\nFor each survey loop in today's `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-22_deployment.db` (today had multiple loops of an 8-line × 58 m pattern at 2 m spacing, then a tighter 16-line × 58 m pattern at 1 m spacing):\n\n1. Extract the loop's spatial footprint (bounding polygon of the boat track + segmentation footprint if available).\n2. Compute the effective surveyed area (account for swath overlap and segmentation FoV).\n3. Pair with the voltage delta over the loop window (ΔV proxy for energy used).\n4. Report area-per-ΔV (or area-per-Ah if current can be derived from the [`#162`/power-analysis-issue voltage-sag model](#TBD)).\n\nCompare loops to surface:\n\n- **Efficiency vs line spacing** (2 m vs 1 m today — more turns per area at 1 m, so more thrust transients per m², expect lower efficiency)\n- **Efficiency vs speed** if multiple loops ran at different speeds\n- **Efficiency vs SOC** (does the boat get more efficient at higher SOC?)\n\n## Class-planning output\n\nA simple table the instructor can use:\n\n| Pattern | Speed | Spacing | m² per loop | ΔV per loop | Estimated loops per battery from 100% SOC |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\nDrives between-cohort battery-swap timing for Lake Massabesic surveys.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Bag data from #160 (already in `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-05-22_deployment.db`)\n- Battery characterization from the comprehensive power-analysis issue (sister to this one). If that's done first, this is a small ride-on; if done in parallel, both share the voltage-curve data.\n\nScope: **small** — sub-week analysis with the bag DB already in place.\n\nPart of #160.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}